@prefix :      <https://thesis.local/kg/portfolio#> .
@prefix xsd:   <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix rdfs:  <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .

#################################################################
# Portfolio Knowledge Graph — Veto Rule Catalog (10 active selection rules + 6 GUARD rules; 8 superseded definitions: the 7 original tree rules and the pre-2026-10-10 LIQUIDITY_DISTRESS)
#
# Loads into named graph urn:graph:rules:catalog.
#
# TOPOLOGY ADDENDUM: 07-ontology-topology.md's original named-graph
# table didn't assign the rule catalog a graph of its own (rules
# were discussed only in the abstract, via the single VETO_COMP_01
# example in 06-ontology-definition.md §1.5). Resolved during
# implementation: rules are versioned by their own validFrom/validTo
# already, but still deserve a dedicated graph so "which ruleset was
# loaded as of transaction-time X" stays answerable the same way
# every other reference-like dataset in this system is — see
# schema/README.md.
#
# (Original header, now describing only the seven SUPERSEDED rules.)
# All 6 rules from v1's catalog table (§4), corrected for the
# unparenthesized ∧/∨ precedence ambiguity (critique #1): every
# confluent rule below is AND(primary_signal, OR(secondary_signals))
# — the intended reading, now structurally the ONLY possible reading
# because there is no infix string left to mis-parse.
#
# Encoding this full catalog (not just VETO_COMP_01) surfaced a
# genuine gap in the original ThresholdComparison-only leaf design:
# VETO_LEG_01/VETO_COMP_02 gate on RiskEvent.category/severity
# (categorical, not numeric) and VETO_RED_01 gates on a graph-
# structural predicate, not a scalar comparison at all. Hence
# CategoricalComparison and GraphPredicate in tbox.ttl.
#################################################################

#################################################################
# ACTIVE RULE CATALOG (T-103, implemented 2026-10-03) — upstream's six rules;
# T-187 (2026-10-13) brings it to nine (read from their code at 6a80ec3, the
# nine-rule table in SPEC.md §2.6, seventh reply)
#
# Maintainer decision (SPEC.md §2.6 D4): portfolio-financial-analysis's
# cycle/rules/builtin.py is the final catalog. Each rule is a flat
# threshold/predicate, so each is a RuleDefinition whose hasClause is a
# single leaf (no RuleClause node) — the tree representation is kept, it
# just degenerates, exactly as VETO_FIN_01 already did. :ruleId is
# upstream's rule_id verbatim, so v_veto.rule_id / v_rule_catalog.rule_id
# resolve to a :RuleDefinition via :ruleId (the :appliesRule target).
#
# What the graph records vs. what upstream evaluates: the leaf is the
# rule's headline condition (v_rule_catalog.param_metric/op/threshold).
# Evaluation stays upstream; branches that do not fit one leaf (e.g.
# LEVERAGE_EXTREME's negative-equity guard) are described in rdfs:comment
# rather than re-encoded, so the graph never claims logic it cannot run.
#
# :priorityRank has no upstream counterpart; it follows upstream's RULES
# list order and only matters for picking :primaryRule.
# :ruleSeverity is upstream's rule_catalog.severity (HARD | SOFT).
# metricName values for upstream metrics are upstream's own identifiers
# and compare against that metric's raw value (see tbox.ttl).
# validFrom is the adoption date, not upstream's created_at, for the first six rules and the seven superseded
# ones. T-187's rows are the exception: they start on 2026-10-10, the day the redefined LIQUIDITY_DISTRESS
# took effect (upstream's merge b3c7661, SPEC.md §2.6 (4c)), so a stint raised from then on resolves. That the
# three NEW rules took effect the same day is assumed (they came with the same contract version 11); T-191 ask (7).
#
# T-187: :penaltyPoints is upstream's penalty_points, set on the SOFT
# rules only (a HARD rule excludes the asset, so upstream's is null and
# there is no triple). Every SOFT rule costs the run's soft_veto_penalty
# (15) unless it declares its own; only BREAK_TREND_200 does, with 0.
# Evaluation stays upstream. LEAF KINDS (flagged in schema/README.md as
# the earlier gaps were): the three new rules and the "could not tell" and
# sector-median branches do not fit a threshold on a raw value, so each is
# a :GraphPredicate named for the condition and "evaluated upstream", as
# DATA_QUALITY already is; the graph does not claim logic it cannot run.
#################################################################

:Rule_LEVERAGE_EXTREME a :RuleDefinition ;
    :ruleId "LEVERAGE_EXTREME" ; :category "FINANCIAL" ; :priorityRank 1 ;
    :ruleSeverity "HARD" ; :validFrom "2026-10-02"^^xsd:date ;
    :hasClause :Cmp_LEVERAGE_EXTREME_DebtToEquity ;
    rdfs:label "Extreme leverage"@en ;
    rdfs:label "Apalancamiento extremo"@es ;
    rdfs:comment "Debt/equity above 3 with positive equity; with non-positive equity, EBITDA <= 0 with net debt, net debt/EBITDA > 5 or interest coverage < 1.5. Does not apply to financial firms."@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Deuda/patrimonio > 3 con patrimonio positivo; con patrimonio no positivo, EBITDA <= 0 con deuda neta, deuda neta/EBITDA > 5 o cobertura de intereses < 1,5. No aplica a empresas financieras."@es .
:Cmp_LEVERAGE_EXTREME_DebtToEquity a :ThresholdComparison ;
    :metricName "leverage.debt_to_equity" ; :operator ">" ; :thresholdValue "3.0"^^xsd:decimal .

:Rule_NEGATIVE_FCF a :RuleDefinition ;
    :ruleId "NEGATIVE_FCF" ; :category "FINANCIAL" ; :priorityRank 2 ;
    :ruleSeverity "HARD" ; :validFrom "2026-10-02"^^xsd:date ;
    :hasClause :Cmp_NEGATIVE_FCF_Margin ;
    rdfs:label "Negative free cash flow"@en ;
    rdfs:label "Flujo de caja libre negativo"@es ;
    rdfs:comment "Trailing-twelve-month free-cash-flow margin below zero. Does not apply to regulated utilities or equity REITs."@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Margen de flujo de caja libre de los últimos doce meses menor que cero. No aplica a utilities reguladas ni a REIT."@es .
:Cmp_NEGATIVE_FCF_Margin a :ThresholdComparison ;
    :metricName "cashflow.free_cash_flow_margin" ; :operator "<" ; :thresholdValue "0.0"^^xsd:decimal .

:Rule_LIQUIDITY_DISTRESS a :RuleDefinition ;
    :ruleId "LIQUIDITY_DISTRESS" ; :category "FINANCIAL" ; :priorityRank 3 ;
    :ruleSeverity "SOFT" ; :penaltyPoints "15"^^xsd:decimal ; :validFrom "2026-10-02"^^xsd:date ;
    :validTo "2026-10-10"^^xsd:date ;
    :hasClause :Cmp_LIQUIDITY_DISTRESS_CurrentRatio ;
    rdfs:label "Liquidity distress"@en ;
    rdfs:label "Estrés de liquidez"@es ;
    rdfs:comment "Superseded on 2026-10-10: current ratio below 1.0 alone. Kept closed with validTo so a stint raised before that date resolves to the definition in force."@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Reemplazada el 2026-10-10: razón corriente inferior a 1,0 por sí sola. Se conserva cerrada con validTo para que un período abierto antes de esa fecha resuelva a la definición vigente."@es .
:Cmp_LIQUIDITY_DISTRESS_CurrentRatio a :ThresholdComparison ;
    :metricName "liquidity.current_ratio" ; :operator "<" ; :thresholdValue "1.0"^^xsd:decimal .

# Redefined in upstream's merge b3c7661 (2026-10-10; no date cut-off in their data, each run rewrites the
# catalog row in place): current ratio below 1.0 AND (interest coverage below 1.5 OR operating cash-flow
# margin below 0). Same :ruleId, a new IRI; a Veto stint resolves to the definition valid on its :raisedOn.
:Rule_LIQUIDITY_DISTRESS_v11 a :RuleDefinition ;
    :ruleId "LIQUIDITY_DISTRESS" ; :category "FINANCIAL" ; :priorityRank 3 ;
    :ruleSeverity "SOFT" ; :penaltyPoints "15"^^xsd:decimal ; :validFrom "2026-10-10"^^xsd:date ;
    :hasClause :Clause_LIQUIDITY_DISTRESS_v11_Root ;
    rdfs:label "Liquidity distress"@en ;
    rdfs:label "Estrés de liquidez"@es ;
    rdfs:comment "Current ratio below 1.0 and (interest coverage below 1.5 or operating cash-flow margin below 0). Does not apply to financial firms or regulated utilities; \"could not tell\" is an upstream evaluation state and the stint stays open."@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Razón corriente < 1,0 y (cobertura de intereses < 1,5 o margen de flujo operativo < 0). No aplica a financieras ni a utilities reguladas; \"no se pudo determinar\" es un estado de evaluación upstream y el período sigue abierto."@es .
:Clause_LIQUIDITY_DISTRESS_v11_Root a :RuleClause ; :clauseType "AND" ;
    :operand1 :Cmp_LIQUIDITY_DISTRESS_v11_CurrentRatio ; :operand2 :Clause_LIQUIDITY_DISTRESS_v11_Coverage .
:Clause_LIQUIDITY_DISTRESS_v11_Coverage a :RuleClause ; :clauseType "OR" ;
    :operand1 :Cmp_LIQUIDITY_DISTRESS_v11_InterestCoverage ; :operand2 :Cmp_LIQUIDITY_DISTRESS_v11_OcfMargin .
:Cmp_LIQUIDITY_DISTRESS_v11_CurrentRatio a :ThresholdComparison ;
    :metricName "liquidity.current_ratio" ; :operator "<" ; :thresholdValue "1.0"^^xsd:decimal .
:Cmp_LIQUIDITY_DISTRESS_v11_InterestCoverage a :ThresholdComparison ;
    :metricName "leverage.interest_coverage" ; :operator "<" ; :thresholdValue "1.5"^^xsd:decimal .
:Cmp_LIQUIDITY_DISTRESS_v11_OcfMargin a :ThresholdComparison ;
    :metricName "cashflow.operating_cash_flow_margin" ; :operator "<" ; :thresholdValue "0.0"^^xsd:decimal .

:Rule_PRICE_CRASH a :RuleDefinition ;
    :ruleId "PRICE_CRASH" ; :category "MARKET" ; :priorityRank 4 ;
    :ruleSeverity "SOFT" ; :penaltyPoints "15"^^xsd:decimal ; :validFrom "2026-10-02"^^xsd:date ;
    :hasClause :Cmp_PRICE_CRASH_Drawdown90d ;
    rdfs:label "Deep 90-day drawdown"@en ;
    rdfs:label "Caída profunda de 90 días"@es ;
    rdfs:comment "90-day maximum drawdown worse than -35%. max_drawdown_90d is a price-derived metric computed upstream."@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Caída máxima de 90 días peor que -35 %. max_drawdown_90d es una métrica derivada de precios calculada upstream."@es .
:Cmp_PRICE_CRASH_Drawdown90d a :ThresholdComparison ;
    :metricName "max_drawdown_90d" ; :operator "<" ; :thresholdValue "-0.35"^^xsd:decimal .

:Rule_EARNINGS_MISSING a :RuleDefinition ;
    :ruleId "EARNINGS_MISSING" ; :category "FINANCIAL" ; :priorityRank 5 ;
    :ruleSeverity "SOFT" ; :penaltyPoints "15"^^xsd:decimal ; :validFrom "2026-10-02"^^xsd:date ;
    :hasClause :Cmp_EARNINGS_MISSING_Age ;
    rdfs:label "Stale fundamentals"@en ;
    rdfs:label "Fundamentales desactualizados"@es ;
    rdfs:comment "A fundamental score exists but its latest filing is older than 400 days. An asset that never had a fundamental score is ineligible upstream, not vetoed by this rule."@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Existe puntaje fundamental, pero el último informe tiene más de 400 días. Un activo que nunca tuvo puntaje fundamental es inelegible upstream, no vetado por esta regla."@es .
:Cmp_EARNINGS_MISSING_Age a :ThresholdComparison ;
    :metricName "fundamental_score_age_days" ; :operator ">" ; :thresholdValue "400"^^xsd:decimal .

:Rule_DATA_QUALITY a :RuleDefinition ;
    :ruleId "DATA_QUALITY" ; :category "DATA_QUALITY" ; :priorityRank 6 ;
    :ruleSeverity "HARD" ; :validFrom "2026-10-02"^^xsd:date ;
    :hasClause :Pred_DATA_QUALITY_HardGate ;
    rdfs:label "Data-quality failure"@en ;
    rdfs:label "Falla de calidad de datos"@es ;
    rdfs:comment "A HARD Ring-1 data-quality gate fired on the asset's latest filing; the evidence is the data_quality_issue row."@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Una verificación dura de calidad de datos del anillo 1 (Ring 1) falló en el último informe del activo; la evidencia es la fila data_quality_issue."@es .
:Pred_DATA_QUALITY_HardGate a :GraphPredicate ; :predicateName "HasHardDataQualityIssue" ;
    rdfs:comment "Upstream params: source=data_quality_issue, severity=HARD. Evaluated upstream." .

# --- T-187: the three rules upstream added with contract version 11, valid from 2026-10-10, the date of their
# merge b3c7661, so a stint raised from then on resolves (ranks 7 to 9 follow the order of
# the seventh reply's table; upstream gives no order, so the ranks are ours) ---
# metric ids (vol_5d, vol_60d_base, ret_5d, mu_60d_base, sma_200) are upstream's daily log-return and price
# figures, computed upstream; none is a :PriceObservation property (T-183 (3) leaves the price columns unread).

:Rule_VOLATILITY_SHOCK a :RuleDefinition ;
    :ruleId "VOLATILITY_SHOCK" ; :category "MARKET" ; :priorityRank 7 ;
    :ruleSeverity "HARD" ; :validFrom "2026-10-10"^^xsd:date ;
    :hasClause :Pred_VOLATILITY_SHOCK ;
    rdfs:label "Volatility shock"@en ;
    rdfs:label "Choque de volatilidad"@es ;
    rdfs:comment "Temporary HARD: 5-session log-return volatility divided by a 60-session baseline ending 5 sessions earlier is above 2.5 and above 2.5 times the sector median that day (fewer than 5 names: the cross-section median). Opens for 10 sessions and renews if the condition persists; evaluated upstream."@en ;
    rdfs:comment "HARD temporal: la volatilidad de retornos logarítmicos de 5 sesiones dividida por una base de 60 sesiones que termina 5 sesiones antes es mayor que 2,5 y mayor que 2,5 veces la mediana sectorial de ese día (menos de 5 nombres: mediana de la sección transversal). Se abre por 10 sesiones y se renueva si la condición persiste; evaluada upstream."@es .
:Pred_VOLATILITY_SHOCK a :GraphPredicate ; :predicateName "VolatilityShock" ;
    rdfs:comment "A label chosen here, not an upstream identifier. Evaluated upstream: vol_5d / vol_60d_base > 2.5 and above 2.5x the sector-median ratio (T-187)." .

:Rule_CRASH_Z_SCORE a :RuleDefinition ;
    :ruleId "CRASH_Z_SCORE" ; :category "MARKET" ; :priorityRank 8 ;
    :ruleSeverity "HARD" ; :validFrom "2026-10-10"^^xsd:date ;
    :hasClause :Pred_CRASH_Z_SCORE ;
    rdfs:label "Abnormal price drop"@en ;
    rdfs:label "Caída anormal de precio"@es ;
    rdfs:comment "Temporary HARD: z = (ret_5d - 5*mu_60d)/(sigma_60d*sqrt(5)) below -2.5 and the same test against the sector median 5-day return below -2.5, with the asset's own 60-session sigma. Same 10-session persistence as VOLATILITY_SHOCK; evaluated upstream."@en ;
    rdfs:comment "HARD temporal: z = (ret_5d - 5*mu_60d)/(sigma_60d*sqrt(5)) inferior a -2,5 y la misma prueba contra la mediana sectorial del retorno de 5 días inferior a -2,5, con la sigma de 60 sesiones de la propia acción. Misma persistencia de 10 sesiones que VOLATILITY_SHOCK; evaluada upstream."@es .
:Pred_CRASH_Z_SCORE a :GraphPredicate ; :predicateName "CrashZScore" ;
    rdfs:comment "A label chosen here, not an upstream identifier. Evaluated upstream: the 5-day return's z-score against its 60-day baseline below -2.5, and the same against the sector median (T-187)." .

:Rule_BREAK_TREND_200 a :RuleDefinition ;
    :ruleId "BREAK_TREND_200" ; :category "MARKET" ; :priorityRank 9 ;
    :ruleSeverity "SOFT" ; :penaltyPoints "0"^^xsd:decimal ; :validFrom "2026-10-10"^^xsd:date ;
    :hasClause :Pred_BREAK_TREND_200 ;
    rdfs:label "Below 200-day trend (flag only)"@en ;
    rdfs:label "Bajo la tendencia de 200 días (solo indicador)"@es ;
    rdfs:comment "Flag only: close more than 5% below its 200-session simple moving average. It marks the name but neither excludes it nor subtracts points; never say it was vetoed."@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Solo indicador: cierre más de 5 % por debajo de su media simple de 200 sesiones. Marca la acción pero no la excluye ni resta puntos; nunca decir que fue vetada."@es .
:Pred_BREAK_TREND_200 a :GraphPredicate ; :predicateName "BelowSma200Band" ;
    rdfs:comment "A label chosen here, not an upstream identifier. Evaluated upstream: close < 0.95 * sma_200 (T-187)." .

# --- T-206 (Contract v18 handoff §5, T-071): the tenth selection rule. It is HARD and applies
# only to regulated utilities (APP-00 company profile). priorityRank 10 is ours (upstream gives no
# order, like T-187's 7-9). validFrom 2026-10-14 is the day T-071 part 2a (PR #167, merge commit
# 7ae8ba8) reached upstream master, 2026-10-14 20:51:47 -0500 (already 2026-10-15 in UTC); T-216
# supplied that real date. It was 2026-10-31, the last safe date, until T-216. It is NOT backdated
# to 2019 or 2020: the other nine rules carry adoption dates (2026-08-13, 2026-10-02, 2026-10-10),
# and valid-time here means when a definition was in force in production (T-187, T-201), not that a
# backtest applies a rule retroactively. The 2022-03-03 veto in the P1 backtest comes from the
# backtest replaying history with today's catalog, which is why backtest vetoes cannot resolve
# their rule by raisedOn (T-209). Upstream's v_rule_catalog.created_at (2026-10-31T19:37:32) is a
# technical persistence timestamp, not the adoption date. The profile exemption is described in
# the comment, not encoded (CategoricalComparison only tests equality).
:Rule_UTILITY_CASH_COVERAGE a :RuleDefinition ;
    :ruleId "UTILITY_CASH_COVERAGE" ; :category "FINANCIAL" ; :priorityRank 10 ;
    :ruleSeverity "HARD" ; :validFrom "2026-10-14"^^xsd:date ;
    :hasClause :Cmp_UTILITY_CASH_COVERAGE_3y ;
    rdfs:label "Weak operating cash flow to debt (regulated utilities)"@en ;
    rdfs:label "Flujo operativo débil frente a la deuda (utilities reguladas)"@es ;
    rdfs:comment "Applies only to regulated utilities: 3-year average operating cash flow before working capital divided by total debt below 5%. HARD."@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Aplica solo a utilities reguladas: flujo operativo medio de tres años antes de capital de trabajo dividido por la deuda total inferior al 5 %. HARD."@es .
:Cmp_UTILITY_CASH_COVERAGE_3y a :ThresholdComparison ;
    :metricName "rule_input.utility_cash_coverage_3y" ; :operator "<" ; :thresholdValue "0.05"^^xsd:decimal .

#################################################################
# GUARD DAILY PROTECTION LAYERS (T-206, Contract v18 handoff §5)
#
# Seven RuleDefinition individuals, one per GUARD rule id, in a
# separate section because they are NOT veto rules: they never
# exclude an asset from the book and are never the object of a
# Veto's :appliesRule/:primaryRule (VetoShape refuses them).
# Each has a single GraphPredicate leaf evaluated upstream, like
# T-187's new rules. :category "GUARD" is what RuleDefinitionShape
# uses to accept them without :ruleSeverity, :penaltyPoints or
# :priorityRank: they carry none of the three. :guardLayer is the
# protection layer: 0 for the portfolio tail-risk events of the Veto
# Hierarchy and 1 for the Basing Points stop/blocked/reentry rules.
# The frozen parameters and academic sources live only in
# rdfs:comment; nothing in this repo runs them.
# L1_BP_STOP/L1_BP_REENTRY are Basing Points guard rules added by
# Work item 33; L0_* and L1_BP_STOP_BLOCKED are the new Veto Hierarchy
# rules of Work item 46. They are valid from 2019-01-02, the GUARD
# calibration-window convention, so a 2022 alert resolves.
# The old L1_STOP_LOSS, L1_REENTRY, L2_NEWS, L3_VOL and L4_DD rules
# were removed by Work item 46; their history belongs in the thesis
# report, not in the graph. Do not load this rules.ttl in production
# before the final reload: the current final alerts still reference
# the removed rules.
#
# validFrom is the start of the calibration window, not an adoption
# date: these are backtest mechanisms, not upstream catalog rows, and
# a GUARD alert in P1-P3 must resolve to a rule valid on its date.
# Confirmed by the upstream maintainer: the calibration window is
# 2019-01-02 to 2021-12-31 (757 NYSE sessions, params.frozen.toml) and
# the date covers every alert and action of P1, P2 and P3.
#################################################################

:Rule_L1_BP_STOP a :RuleDefinition ;
    :ruleId "L1_BP_STOP" ; :category "GUARD" ; :guardLayer 1 ;
    :validFrom "2026-11-04"^^xsd:date ;
    :hasClause :Pred_L1_BP_STOP ;
    rdfs:label "Exit by Basing Points rule"@en ;
    rdfs:label "Salida por regla Basing Points"@es ;
    rdfs:comment "Layer 1 of the System: a satellite name goes to cash when its close falls below its rising Basing Points stop (latest Basing Point low times (1 - d), with d from Edwards' Table of Stop Distances and the 252-session beta); the name stays out until the next decision date."@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Capa 1 del Sistema: una acción del satélite pasa a efectivo cuando su cierre cae por debajo de su stop Basing Points creciente (último mínimo Basing Point por (1 - d), con d de la tabla de distancias de Edwards y la beta de 252 sesiones); la acción queda fuera hasta la siguiente fecha de decisión."@es .
:Pred_L1_BP_STOP a :GraphPredicate ; :predicateName "GuardBasingPointsStop" ;
    rdfs:comment "A label chosen here, not an upstream identifier. Evaluated upstream: close below the rising Basing Points stop (latest Basing Point low × (1 − d))." .

:Rule_L1_BP_REENTRY a :RuleDefinition ;
    :ruleId "L1_BP_REENTRY" ; :category "GUARD" ; :guardLayer 1 ;
    :validFrom "2026-11-04"^^xsd:date ;
    :hasClause :Pred_L1_BP_REENTRY ;
    rdfs:label "Re-entry after Basing Points exit"@en ;
    rdfs:label "Reentrada tras salida Basing Points"@es ;
    rdfs:comment "At a decision date, a name stopped by L1_BP_STOP that is still selected re-enters with a fresh Basing Points machine."@en ;
    rdfs:comment "En una fecha de decisión, una acción detenida por L1_BP_STOP que sigue seleccionada reentra con una máquina Basing Points nueva."@es .
:Pred_L1_BP_REENTRY a :GraphPredicate ; :predicateName "GuardBasingPointsReentry" ;
    rdfs:comment "A label chosen here, not an upstream identifier. Evaluated upstream: a stopped satellite that is still selected re-enters with a fresh Basing Points machine." .

:Rule_L0_CARTERA_ACTIVATION a :RuleDefinition ;
    :ruleId "L0_CARTERA_ACTIVATION" ; :category "GUARD" ; :guardLayer 0 ;
    :validFrom "2019-01-02"^^xsd:date ;
    :hasClause :Pred_L0_CARTERA_ACTIVATION ;
    rdfs:label "Portfolio tail-risk activation"@en ;
    rdfs:label "Activación del riesgo de cola de la cartera"@es ;
    rdfs:comment "Layer 0 of the Veto Hierarchy: the portfolio's 63-session CVaR95 crosses the 80th percentile of its previous 252 values; the exposure scale leaves 1."@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Capa 0 de la Jerarquía de Veto: el CVaR95 a 63 sesiones de la cartera cruza el percentil 80 de sus 252 valores anteriores; la escala de exposición deja 1."@es .
:Pred_L0_CARTERA_ACTIVATION a :GraphPredicate ; :predicateName "GuardPortfolioTailRiskActivation" ;
    rdfs:comment "A label chosen here, not an upstream identifier. Evaluated upstream: portfolio CVaR95 above its 80th-percentile threshold." .

:Rule_L0_CARTERA_SCALE_CHANGE a :RuleDefinition ;
    :ruleId "L0_CARTERA_SCALE_CHANGE" ; :category "GUARD" ; :guardLayer 0 ;
    :validFrom "2019-01-02"^^xsd:date ;
    :hasClause :Pred_L0_CARTERA_SCALE_CHANGE ;
    rdfs:label "Portfolio tail-risk scale change"@en ;
    rdfs:label "Cambio de escala del riesgo de cola de la cartera"@es ;
    rdfs:comment "Layer 0 of the Veto Hierarchy: a scale already below 1 changes again as the portfolio's tail risk moves."@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Capa 0 de la Jerarquía de Veto: una escala ya inferior a 1 cambia de nuevo cuando se mueve el riesgo de cola de la cartera."@es .
:Pred_L0_CARTERA_SCALE_CHANGE a :GraphPredicate ; :predicateName "GuardPortfolioScaleChange" ;
    rdfs:comment "A label chosen here, not an upstream identifier. Evaluated upstream: a scale change with s_old < 1." .

:Rule_L0_CARTERA_RECOVERY a :RuleDefinition ;
    :ruleId "L0_CARTERA_RECOVERY" ; :category "GUARD" ; :guardLayer 0 ;
    :validFrom "2019-01-02"^^xsd:date ;
    :hasClause :Pred_L0_CARTERA_RECOVERY ;
    rdfs:label "Portfolio tail-risk recovery"@en ;
    rdfs:label "Recuperación del riesgo de cola de la cartera"@es ;
    rdfs:comment "Layer 0 of the Veto Hierarchy: the exposure scale returns to 1 when the portfolio risk ratio is at most 0.90."@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Capa 0 de la Jerarquía de Veto: la escala de exposición vuelve a 1 cuando la razón de riesgo de la cartera es como máximo 0,90."@es .
:Pred_L0_CARTERA_RECOVERY a :GraphPredicate ; :predicateName "GuardPortfolioScaleRecovery" ;
    rdfs:comment "A label chosen here, not an upstream identifier. Evaluated upstream: the scale returns to 1." .

:Rule_L1_BP_STOP_BLOCKED a :RuleDefinition ;
    :ruleId "L1_BP_STOP_BLOCKED" ; :category "GUARD" ; :guardLayer 1 ;
    :validFrom "2019-01-02"^^xsd:date ;
    :hasClause :Pred_L1_BP_STOP_BLOCKED ;
    rdfs:label "Blocked Basing Points stop"@en ;
    rdfs:label "Parada Basing Points bloqueada"@es ;
    rdfs:comment "Layer 1 of the Veto Hierarchy: a name in the stop memory is blocked at a decision because its close is still below the stored level; it is kept out of the candidate set. Neither the close nor the stored level is loaded."@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Capa 1 de la Jerarquía de Veto: un nombre en la memoria de la parada queda bloqueado en una decisión porque su cierre sigue por debajo del nivel guardado; queda fuera del conjunto de candidatas. Ni el cierre ni el nivel guardado se cargan."@es .
:Pred_L1_BP_STOP_BLOCKED a :GraphPredicate ; :predicateName "GuardBasingPointsStopBlocked" ;
    rdfs:comment "A label chosen here, not an upstream identifier. Evaluated upstream: a stopped name is blocked at a decision while its close is below the stored level." .

#################################################################
# SUPERSEDED — the original seven tree rules (design history)
#
# Closed with :validTo 2026-10-02 (never deleted, per the valid-time
# convention) so the dated worked example in instances.trig keeps
# resolving :appliesRule. They are no longer the target catalog and
# must not be extended; VETO_RED_01's contagion rule has no upstream
# counterpart and is dropped. The original header (v1 catalog, AND/OR
# trees) is at the top of this file and describes only these seven.
#################################################################

# --- Rank 1: VETO_LEG_01 — Legal, single rule, AND of two categorical checks ---
:Rule_VETO_LEG_01 a :RuleDefinition ;
    :ruleId "VETO_LEG_01" ; :category "LEGAL" ; :priorityRank 1 ;
    :validFrom "2026-01-01"^^xsd:date ;
    :validTo "2026-10-02"^^xsd:date ;
    :hasClause :Clause_LEG01_Root .

:Clause_LEG01_Root a :RuleClause ; :clauseType "AND" ;
    :operand1 :Cat_LEG01_Category ; :operand2 :Cat_LEG01_Severity .

:Cat_LEG01_Category a :CategoricalComparison ; :attributeName "category" ; :expectedValue "LEGAL" .
:Cat_LEG01_Severity a :CategoricalComparison ; :attributeName "severity" ; :expectedValue "CRITICAL" .

# --- Rank 2: VETO_FIN_01 — Financial, single signal, tree degenerates to one leaf ---
:Rule_VETO_FIN_01 a :RuleDefinition ;
    :ruleId "VETO_FIN_01" ; :category "FINANCIAL" ; :priorityRank 2 ;
    :validFrom "2026-01-01"^^xsd:date ;
    :validTo "2026-10-02"^^xsd:date ;
    :hasClause :Cmp_FIN01_ScoreHigh .

:Cmp_FIN01_ScoreHigh a :ThresholdComparison ; :metricName "ScoreFinanciero" ; :operator ">" ; :thresholdValue "0.85"^^xsd:decimal .

# --- Rank 3: VETO_COMP_02 — Legal/Reputational, confluent ---
# Corrected: (category=LEGAL AND severity=HIGH) AND (Sentiment<-0.50 OR ScoreCuantitativo>0.65)
:Rule_VETO_COMP_02 a :RuleDefinition ;
    :ruleId "VETO_COMP_02" ; :category "LEGAL_REPUTATIONAL" ; :priorityRank 3 ;
    :validFrom "2026-01-01"^^xsd:date ;
    :validTo "2026-10-02"^^xsd:date ;
    :hasClause :Clause_COMP02_Root .

:Clause_COMP02_Root a :RuleClause ; :clauseType "AND" ;
    :operand1 :Clause_COMP02_LegalHigh ; :operand2 :Clause_COMP02_SentOrQuant .

:Clause_COMP02_LegalHigh a :RuleClause ; :clauseType "AND" ;
    :operand1 :Cat_COMP02_Category ; :operand2 :Cat_COMP02_Severity .
:Cat_COMP02_Category a :CategoricalComparison ; :attributeName "category" ; :expectedValue "LEGAL" .
:Cat_COMP02_Severity a :CategoricalComparison ; :attributeName "severity" ; :expectedValue "HIGH" .

:Clause_COMP02_SentOrQuant a :RuleClause ; :clauseType "OR" ;
    :operand1 :Cmp_COMP02_SentLow ; :operand2 :Cmp_COMP02_QuantHigh .
:Cmp_COMP02_SentLow  a :ThresholdComparison ; :metricName "Sentiment"        ; :operator "<" ; :thresholdValue "-0.50"^^xsd:decimal .
:Cmp_COMP02_QuantHigh a :ThresholdComparison ; :metricName "ScoreCuantitativo" ; :operator ">" ; :thresholdValue "0.65"^^xsd:decimal .

# --- Rank 4: VETO_COMP_01 — Financial/Market, confluent ---
# Corrected: ScoreFinanciero>0.65 AND (Sentiment<-0.60 OR ScoreTecnico>0.70)
:Rule_VETO_COMP_01 a :RuleDefinition ;
    :ruleId "VETO_COMP_01" ; :category "FINANCIAL_MARKET" ; :priorityRank 4 ;
    :validFrom "2026-01-01"^^xsd:date ;
    :validTo "2026-10-02"^^xsd:date ;
    :hasClause :Clause_COMP01_Root .

:Clause_COMP01_Root a :RuleClause ; :clauseType "AND" ;
    :operand1 :Cmp_COMP01_FinHigh ; :operand2 :Clause_COMP01_Inner .

:Clause_COMP01_Inner a :RuleClause ; :clauseType "OR" ;
    :operand1 :Cmp_COMP01_SentLow ; :operand2 :Cmp_COMP01_TecHigh .

:Cmp_COMP01_FinHigh  a :ThresholdComparison ; :metricName "ScoreFinanciero" ; :operator ">" ; :thresholdValue "0.65"^^xsd:decimal .
:Cmp_COMP01_SentLow  a :ThresholdComparison ; :metricName "Sentiment"       ; :operator "<" ; :thresholdValue "-0.60"^^xsd:decimal .
:Cmp_COMP01_TecHigh  a :ThresholdComparison ; :metricName "ScoreTecnico"    ; :operator ">" ; :thresholdValue "0.70"^^xsd:decimal .

# --- Rank 5: VETO_RED_01 — Network/Contagion, confluent, graph-structural primary signal ---
# Corrected: HasSharedPrimaryVetoExecutive(A) AND (Sentiment<-0.50 OR ScoreFinanciero>0.65)
:Rule_VETO_RED_01 a :RuleDefinition ;
    :ruleId "VETO_RED_01" ; :category "NETWORK" ; :priorityRank 5 ;
    :validFrom "2026-01-01"^^xsd:date ;
    :validTo "2026-10-02"^^xsd:date ;
    :hasClause :Clause_RED01_Root .

:Clause_RED01_Root a :RuleClause ; :clauseType "AND" ;
    :operand1 :Pred_RED01_SharedExec ; :operand2 :Clause_RED01_Inner .

:Pred_RED01_SharedExec a :GraphPredicate ; :predicateName "HasSharedPrimaryVetoExecutive" ;
    rdfs:comment "Evaluated by the Orchestrator against sharedExecutiveWith + the T-1 checkpointed prior-cycle Veto state (08-agent-architecture.md), excluding primary vetoes triggered by VETO_RED_01 itself (de-recursion, v1 §4). T-107: sharedExecutiveWith is now reserved for VERIFIED edges and no upstream source produces them, so this closed design-history predicate has no feed; upstream's news candidates (:AssetCoOccurrence) do not drive it." .

:Clause_RED01_Inner a :RuleClause ; :clauseType "OR" ;
    :operand1 :Cmp_RED01_SentLow ; :operand2 :Cmp_RED01_FinHigh .
:Cmp_RED01_SentLow a :ThresholdComparison ; :metricName "Sentiment"        ; :operator "<" ; :thresholdValue "-0.50"^^xsd:decimal .
:Cmp_RED01_FinHigh a :ThresholdComparison ; :metricName "ScoreFinanciero"  ; :operator ">" ; :thresholdValue "0.65"^^xsd:decimal .

# --- Rank 6: VETO_COMP_03 — Market/Volatility, confluent, already unambiguous (pure AND) ---
:Rule_VETO_COMP_03 a :RuleDefinition ;
    :ruleId "VETO_COMP_03" ; :category "MARKET_VOLATILITY" ; :priorityRank 6 ;
    :validFrom "2026-01-01"^^xsd:date ;
    :validTo "2026-10-02"^^xsd:date ;
    :hasClause :Clause_COMP03_Root .

:Clause_COMP03_Root a :RuleClause ; :clauseType "AND" ;
    :operand1 :Cmp_COMP03_QuantHigh ; :operand2 :Cmp_COMP03_TecHigh .
:Cmp_COMP03_QuantHigh a :ThresholdComparison ; :metricName "ScoreCuantitativo" ; :operator ">" ; :thresholdValue "0.75"^^xsd:decimal .
:Cmp_COMP03_TecHigh   a :ThresholdComparison ; :metricName "ScoreTecnico"      ; :operator ">" ; :thresholdValue "0.75"^^xsd:decimal .

# --- Rank 7: VETO_MKT_02 — Market/Sector-Momentum, single signal (added 2026-08-13) ---
# Design history (T-155): its -0.50 threshold is on SectorRelativeMomentum's original [-1, 1] scale. The shape
# now allows [-100, 100] (upstream's TECHNICAL points), so do not reuse or extend this rule as written.
# Closes part of critique #3 (sector layer) — see docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-13-
# attractiveness-sector-momentum-design.md. Appended after the original 6; none of their
# already-validated thresholds change.
:Rule_VETO_MKT_02 a :RuleDefinition ;
    :ruleId "VETO_MKT_02" ; :category "MARKET" ; :priorityRank 7 ;
    :validFrom "2026-08-13"^^xsd:date ;
    :validTo "2026-10-02"^^xsd:date ;
    :hasClause :Cmp_MKT02_SectorMomentumLow .

:Cmp_MKT02_SectorMomentumLow a :ThresholdComparison ;
    :metricName "SectorRelativeMomentum" ; :operator "<" ; :thresholdValue "-0.50"^^xsd:decimal ;
    rdfs:comment "Compared via rawValue, not normalizedScore — SectorRelativeMomentum is a signed delta, same raw-scale convention as Sentiment (see tbox.ttl's ThresholdComparison comment). Placeholder threshold pending calibration (B5), same status as every other threshold in this file." .

#################################################################
# Attractiveness weight scheme (added 2026-08-13) — the positive
# counterpart to this rule catalog. WeightScheme_v1 is versioned graph
# data, same pattern as RuleDefinition above (critique #6's principle
# applied to weights, not just thresholds). Since T-121 an upstream
# scheme is NOT versioned: it is one cycle_run, dated by :cycleDate,
# never closed, and written to urn:graph:ingest:ORCHESTRATOR:{date},
# not to this catalog. Design history (T-155): the blend
# this scheme once fed is computed upstream (portfolio-financial-analysis'
# cycle runner), not here; see the 2026-08-13 design spec, marked as design
# history. Placeholder weights, never applied by this repo.
#################################################################
:WeightScheme_v1 a :AttractivenessWeightScheme ;
    :schemeId "ATTR_WEIGHTS_V1" ; :validFrom "2026-08-13"^^xsd:date ;
    :hasWeightComponent :WC_Fin, :WC_Quant, :WC_Tec, :WC_Sent, :WC_SectorMom .

:WC_Fin       a :WeightComponent ; :weightMetricName "ScoreFinanciero"        ; :weightValue "0.25"^^xsd:decimal ; :inverted true .
:WC_Quant     a :WeightComponent ; :weightMetricName "ScoreCuantitativo"      ; :weightValue "0.20"^^xsd:decimal ; :inverted true .
:WC_Tec       a :WeightComponent ; :weightMetricName "ScoreTecnico"           ; :weightValue "0.20"^^xsd:decimal ; :inverted true .
:WC_Sent      a :WeightComponent ; :weightMetricName "Sentiment"              ; :weightValue "0.20"^^xsd:decimal ; :inverted false .
:WC_SectorMom a :WeightComponent ; :weightMetricName "SectorRelativeMomentum" ; :weightValue "0.15"^^xsd:decimal ; :inverted false .
